<item>
            <title>[LU-20938] sanity test_154i: unchecked mkdir and cd hide EIO as path2fid failure</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20938</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_154i fails with &quot;path2fid failed&quot; on change 69369 patchset 2, review-dne-zfs-part-1, RHEL 10.1 with ZFS and DNE.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failed session: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/58764f53-5586-42ed-97bd-c80cfcc21937&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/58764f53-5586-42ed-97bd-c80cfcc21937&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Failed test set: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7c000439-9943-449d-a11f-029ca70f63a4&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7c000439-9943-449d-a11f-029ca70f63a4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test log: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/8b3d6e15-72ef-4783-8931-d2fef79ad726/show_text&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/8b3d6e15-72ef-4783-8931-d2fef79ad726/show_text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The log starts with:&lt;br/&gt;
mkdir: cannot create directory &apos;/mnt/lustre/d154i.sanity&apos;: Input/output error&lt;br/&gt;
sanity.sh: line 20824: cd: /mnt/lustre/d154i.sanity: No such file or directory&lt;br/&gt;
It then creates the deep relative directory tree and reports:&lt;br/&gt;
lfs path2fid: cannot get fid for &apos;.&apos;: Operation not supported&lt;br/&gt;
sanity test_154i: FAIL: path2fid failed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test does not check its initial mkdir or cd. After setup fails it continues in the original working directory outside Lustre, so the reported path2fid failure hides the original mkdir EIO. Check both setup operations and stop on failure, then investigate the initial EIO. Maloo retained only the suite log, test log and ZFS logs; no dmesg or debug log is available for this failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is pre-existing test code, not introduced by change 69369. That change only batches facet-up checks in failover and quota helpers; test_154i and its directory setup do not use those helpers. Rainshadow records 15 earlier failures of this test with &quot;path2fid failed&quot;, across unrelated reviews from January 2025 through June 2026. Logs on changes 65862/4 and 66247/2 confirm the same path2fid EOPNOTSUPP, though their logs do not show the initial mkdir EIO, so identical underlying causes are not established:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/98b50367-2069-4c55-9736-be231585d6d9&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/98b50367-2069-4c55-9736-be231585d6d9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5ba470b8-ac20-46e5-b134-94fa031c8dce&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5ba470b8-ac20-46e5-b134-94fa031c8dce&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;JIRA searches for test_154i, path2fid failed, d154i.sanity and path2fid with Operation not supported found no covering ticket. &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18294&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_154i: FAIL: fid2path failed (1)&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18294&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18294&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; covers a later fid2path overflow; &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18082&quot; title=&quot;Support paths longer than PATH_MAX for fid2path&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18082&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18082&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; adds long-path fid2path support. &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18569&quot; title=&quot;sanity-sec: timeout - clients lost connection to MGS&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18569&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18569&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is an unrelated sanity-sec connectivity timeout. The other signature matches, &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15777&quot; title=&quot;HSM changelog indicates success for a failed restore&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-15777&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15777&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-8071&quot; title=&quot;lvcreate --snapshot of MDT hangs in ldiskfs_journal_start_sb&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-8071&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-8071&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, concern HSM layout swaps and LVM snapshot hangs respectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69369-ps2-425ed3947678 on &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/69369&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69369&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
